WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
Every cell in your body is wrapped
in a membrane just 2 molecules thick.

2
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.970
The same basic sheet also wraps the
nucleus and the mitochondria inside.

3
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.520
Its molecules are never fixed in place.

4
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.270
They slide sideways past each
other, yet the sheet stays whole.

5
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.780
So why do a membrane's molecules
form that sheet by themselves?

6
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.820
In this mission, you'll
meet the phospholipid:

7
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:29.280
a molecule with a head and two
tails that act very differently.

8
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.100
Then you'll build the whole fluid mosaic:

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.340
proteins scattered through the
sheet, sugar chains on the outside.

10
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: explain why a membrane's
molecules form a sheet two molecules thick,

11
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.000
all by themselves.
